# v34 OVERLAY (user 2026-11-02: "use goal reward for exploration ... sample
# very far off goals i.e. negative mine - goals from different environment but
# give forward reward in every direction moved and then goal reward at 100m";
# mode bit HIDDEN, from scratch, on v33's recipe).
#
# WHY. v29 and v33 both learned to ignore the goal image: goals sit ahead along
# the lane, so lane following alone reaches many of them (v33's wrong-goal
# success climbed 0.000 -> 0.300 by 800k). Here an explore episode is a goal
# episode whose goal is UNREACHABLE -- a view from the other training town --
# and the right behaviour there is to keep driving. With the mode bit hidden,
# only the image tells the policy which case it is in.
. "$REPO/slurm/v33_overlay.env"

# Explore episodes are shown another TRAINING town's goal view (Town05 <->
# Town01; never a held-out eval town). Counted per episode as
# served_foreign_goal / foreign_goal_fallback.
export FOREIGN_GOAL_EXPLORE=1

# The network always sees mode = 1; the true mode still drives the reward, the
# replay flag and HER.
export HIDE_MODE_BIT=1

# THE GOAL REWARD AT 100 m of driving (was +10): explore success now pays the
# same +100 as reaching a goal. Forward progress along the road in whichever
# direction it drives, +1 per metre, is explore's per-step pay as before; the
# +10 per junction cleared stays. Worth up to ~+250, inside the 300 ceiling.
export EXPLORE_ARRIVAL_BONUS=100
